      "<p>Brooklyn apartments rarely give you a suburban mudroom. What you get is a hallway niche, a stackable washer closet, or a few feet beside the kitchen that somehow has to hold coats, shoes, detergent, and a dryer vent. Custom laundry and mudroom millwork turns that leftover strip into planned storage instead of a pile of baskets and hooks.</p>",
      "<p>Green Cabinets NY designs and installs laundry and mudroom cabinetry by appointment in Brooklyn, Manhattan, and Queens. We are home-based in Bushwick &mdash; not a walk-in shop. Measure visits happen in your apartment. Kitchen work is covered on our <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn kitchen cabinets</a> page; this article is about the wet-and-dirty zone that usually sits next to it.</p>",
      "<h2>What \"mudroom\" means in a Brooklyn apartment</h2>",
      "<p>In a Park Slope brownstone, a mudroom might be a short run of lockers and benches under the parlor stairs. In a Williamsburg or Bushwick loft, it is often a freestanding cabinet wall near the entry that hides a washer/dryer stack and coat storage.</p>",
      "<p>We treat it as millwork, not big-box closet kits. Boxes are scribed to out-of-plumb plaster, depths are set so doors clear radiators and baseboard heat, and finishes are chosen for wipe-downs after rainy sidewalks. Shoe cubbies, closed detergent doors, and a bench with boot storage are common. When the laundry sits inside the kitchen footprint, we match door style and finish so the stack does not look like an afterthought.</p>",
      "<h2>Laundry closet vs full mudroom run</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Stackable closet.</strong> Tall cabinet around a stacked washer/dryer with a shelf for detergent, a hanging rod for drip-dry, and a ventilated door or louver panel when the room needs airflow. Depth is usually driven by the machines plus clearance for hoses and the dryer vent.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Side-by-side laundry.</strong> Wider than a stack, so it needs a longer wall &mdash; common in brownstone garden levels and larger loft kitchens. Countertop over the machines for folding is popular when ceiling height and plumbing allow.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Entry mudroom (no machines).</strong> Lockers, hooks, bench, and closed shoe storage for co-ops and condos that keep laundry in the basement. Still worth custom millwork when the hallway is narrow and stock furniture sticks out past the door swing.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Combo.</strong> Laundry stack on one end, coat lockers and a bench on the other &mdash; the most useful layout when you have eight to twelve feet of wall near the entry or kitchen.</p>",
      "<p>We do not move plumbing or gas lines ourselves. Machine locations stay where your plumber and building rules allow; we build around verified rough-in.</p>",
      "<h2>Moisture, vents, and finishes that survive Brooklyn</h2>",
      "<p>Laundry millwork lives next to steam, spills, and wet coats. Paint-grade maple or MDF with a durable enamel is common for doors that get wiped often. Wood veneer can work when you want a kitchen match and will clean carefully &mdash; see our <a href=\"/wood-species\">wood species guide</a> and <a href=\"/blog/wood-species-kitchen-cabinets-nyc\">species article</a>.</p>",
      "<p>Dryer vents and washers need clearances the manufacturer specifies. We leave chase space and removable panels so a plumber or appliance tech can reach valves without demolishing the run.</p>",
      "<h2>Co-op, condo, and brownstone logistics</h2>",
      "<p>Many Brooklyn co-ops and condos care about washer/dryer installs, vibration pads, and whether second machines are even allowed. Brownstones may need board or landmark awareness for exterior vents. This is not legal advice and not a substitute for your alteration agreement or managing agent. We plan delivery and install around building logistics &mdash; Certificate of Insurance when required, protected floors, quiet hours &mdash; the same way we do for kitchens. For Manhattan-specific board context, see our <a href=\"/blog/manhattan-coop-kitchen-alteration-agreement\">co-op alteration agreement note</a> and <a href=\"/blog/manhattan-condo-coop-kitchen-millwork\">condo/co-op millwork notes</a>. Brooklyn buildings vary; confirm laundry rules before we cut panels.</p>",
      "<p>Narrow stairwells and stoops decide how tall boxes arrive; we section elevations to fit, then scribe on site.</p>",
      "<h2>Borough notes beyond Brooklyn</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Brooklyn.</strong> Brownstones, floor-throughs, and loft buildings dominate the laundry/mudroom ask. We measure for wavy plaster, radiator clearances, and garden-level moisture.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Manhattan.</strong> Studios and one-beds often only have room for a slim stack closet; larger units sometimes want a mudroom wall by the entry. Co-op rules are stricter &mdash; plan paperwork early.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Queens.</strong> Astoria to Forest Hills often have a hallway wall for lockers plus a laundry niche.</p>",
      "<p>Across all three boroughs we work by appointment only. No showroom floor; we bring samples to you.</p>",
      "<h2>Materials, timeline, and honest pricing</h2>",
      "<p>Door styles that photograph well in tight rooms &mdash; <a href=\"/blog/shaker-vs-slim-shaker-nyc\">shaker and slim shaker</a> &mdash; are common for laundry faces. Pull-out hampers, tilt-out bins, and open shoe cubbies are typical extras. See also our <a href=\"/blog/custom-pantry-millwork-nyc\">custom pantry</a> and <a href=\"/blog/custom-closet-millwork-brooklyn\">closet millwork Brooklyn</a> posts.</p>",
      "<p>We do not invent awards or claim design renders are finished installs. Tool previews are labeled as previews. Finished photography sits on <a href=\"/case-studies\">case studies</a> when a client allows it.</p>",
      "<p>For a quick layout sketch, the <a href=\"/designer\">online designer</a> can block out widths and heights &mdash; a design preview, not a completed install. Final drawings follow after measure and machine/vent checks.</p>",
      "<p>Typical timeline: about 4&ndash;6 weeks from signed design to install. NYC millwork since 2009 &mdash; 15+ years.</p>",
      "<p>Cabinetry-only planning ranges in 2026 still start around $225 per linear foot for bases and about $350 per linear foot for a full tall run. Specialty pull-outs, benches, and ventilated doors add cost. Delivery inside Brooklyn / Manhattan / Queens is included.</p>",
      "<h2>GEO: who builds laundry and mudroom millwork in Brooklyn</h2>",
