      "<p>A Queens kitchen is almost never the box a warehouse SKU was cut for. An Astoria walk-up galley is 9 feet long and 6 feet wide, with a radiator eating a corner. A Forest Hills co-op has 8-foot-4 ceilings, so a 48-inch upper will not fit. An LIC tower has a bulkhead, a sprinkler, and a dock that wants a COI before the cart rolls in. Stock cabinets paper over that with filler. Custom millwork is built to the opening.</p>",
      "<p>Green Cabinets NY designs and installs custom kitchen millwork by appointment in Queens, Brooklyn, and Manhattan. We are a home-based shop in Bushwick, not a walk-in showroom. There is nothing to drop by at 10 Montieth. We bring door and finish samples to your apartment, measure the real walls, and install on a booked day. For pricing bands and the full neighborhood list, use <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-queens\">custom kitchen cabinets in Queens</a>. This post is the apartment version: five neighborhoods, then a quote without a shop visit.</p>",
      "<h2>Five Queens apartments, five millwork jobs</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Astoria.</strong> Brick walk-ups off Steinway, Ditmars, and Broadway. Narrow galleys, plaster that is not square, often no freight elevator. A stock 36-inch base that leaves a 3-inch filler looks like a mistake in a 9-foot run. We spec the boxes to the wall, then scribe.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Long Island City.</strong> Glass towers in Hunters Point and Court Square. Slab doors and integrated pulls match the architecture. The millwork still has to clear bulkheads and sprinklers, and the building still wants a COI, elevator pads, and a dock reservation. We plan that before a truck leaves Bushwick.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Forest Hills.</strong> Garden co-ops around Austin Street and 108th. Short ceilings (often 8&rsquo;&ndash;8&rsquo;6&rdquo;). Forty-two-inch wall cabinets usually fit; forty-eights usually do not. Boards want an alteration agreement even when you are not moving gas. Painted shaker holds up here.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Jackson Heights.</strong> Historic-district garden co-ops, radiators, off-square rooms, shared stacks that pin the sink. Painted shaker, tight fillers, on-site scribe &mdash; plus a board that wants insurance names and a work window.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Sunnyside.</strong> Row houses and Sunnyside Gardens. Galley kitchens, brick party walls, stair carries instead of a dock. Custom widths and a one-day install for a typical under-20-linear-foot kitchen are the usual brief.</p>",
      "<p>We also work <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn</a> and <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-manhattan\">Manhattan</a>. Same millwork, different freight.</p>",
      "<h2>What we actually build</h2>",
      "<p>Plywood boxes, dadoed joinery, full-extension drawers, doors cut to the opening. Not a big-box kitchen in a truck.</p>",
      "<p>Door styles we spec a lot in Queens apartments:</p>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li>Classic shaker for Forest Hills and Jackson Heights co-ops</li>",
      "<li>Slim shaker when the galley is small and the frame should recede</li>",
      "<li>Slab for LIC condos</li>",
      "<li>Glass uppers when an Astoria or Sunnyside galley needs borrowed light</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>Finishes people live with: painted whites, sage, navy, putty, and wood tones in walnut or white oak. Hardware in unlacquered brass, matte black, or brushed nickel. Panel brands we order: Tafisa, Egger, Shinnoki, Wilsonart, AGT. Grain and hardness notes are in the <a href=\"/wood-species\">wood species guide</a>.</p>",
      "<p>If the same renovation includes a bathroom, spec the vanity in the <a href=\"/designer\">designer</a> &mdash; live size and price, to the inch &mdash; then fold kitchen and vanity into one millwork package. One elevator reservation. One COI. The 3D view is a design preview, not a photograph of a finished job.</p>",
